g all groups and projects, the container registry, the dependency proxy, and the package registry. \\n\\n<::before><::after> read_api \\n\\nGrants read access to the API, including all groups and projects, the container registry, and the package registry. \\n\\n<::before><::after> read_user \\n\\nGrants read-only access to your profile through the /user API endpoint, which includes username, public email, and full name. Also grants access to read-only API endpoints under /users. \\n\\n<::before><::after> create_runner \\n\\nGrants create access to the runners. \\n\\n<::before><::after> manage_runner \\n\\nGrants access to manage the runners. \\n\\n<::before><::after> k8s_proxy \\n\\nGrants permission to perform Kubernetes API calls using the agent for Kubernetes. \\n\\n<::before><::after> read_repository \\n\\nGrants read-only access to repositories on private projects using Git-over-HTTP or the Repository Files API. \\n\\n<::before><::after> write_repository \\n\\nGrants read-write access to repositories on private projects using Git-over-HTTP (not using the API). \\n\\n<::before><::after> ai_features \\n\\nGrants access to GitLab Duo related API endpoints. \\n\\n<::before><::after> sudo \\n\\nGrants permission to perform API actions as any user in the system, when authenticated as an admin user. \\n\\n<::before><::after> admin_mode \\n\\nGrants permission to perform API actions as an administrator, when Admin Mode is enabled. \\n\\n<::before><::after> read_service_ping \\n\\nGrant access to download Service Ping payload via API when authenticated as an admin user \\n\\nCreate personal access token  Cancel \\n\\nToken name  \u2191  (Click to sort ascending)  |  Scopes  \u2191  (Click to sort ascending)  |  Created  \u2191  (Click to sort ascending)  |  Last Used  [ The last time a token was used  ](/help/user/profile/personal_access_tokens.md#view-the-last-time-a-token-was-used) \u2191  (Click to sort ascending)  |  Expires  \u2191  (Click to sort ascending)  |  Action   \\n---|---|---|---|---|---  \\nroot-token  |  api, read_user, read_api, read_repository, write_repository, sudo, admin_mode  |  Nov 18, 2024  |  |  |  [ ](/-/user_settings/personal_access_tokens/1/revoke \"Revoke\")  \\n  \\n<::after>\\n\\n#### \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nFeed token \\n\\nYour feed token authenticates you when your RSS reader loads a personalized RSS feed or when your calendar application loads a personalized calendar. It is visible in those feed URLs. It cannot be used to access any other data. \\n\\nFeed token \\n\\nKeep this token secret. Anyone who has it can read activity and issue RSS feeds or your calendar feed as if they were you. If that happens, [ reset this token ](/-/profile/reset_feed_token) . \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/-/user_settings/personal_access_tokens', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251112_134351_906776.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/-/user_settings/personal_access_tokens'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action='\\n\\n\\nclick(\\'417\\')  # Click on \"Add new token\" button\\nnoop(2000)  # Wait for form to load\\n\\n\\n', last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='67'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"\\n\\nfill('424', 'issue-deletion-token')  # Fill token name\\nnoop(1000)  # Wait\\n\\n\", thought='Great! I can see the form to create a new personal access token. Now I need to fill out the form with the required information. Let me fill in the token name and select the required scopes as per the SOP.', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action=<ActionType.BROWSE_INTERACTIVE: 'browse_interactive'>, security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  *     * [ New project/repository  ](/projects/new)\\n    * [ New grou